A||N||9||Xtreme Fiero's||Turbo/ SC/ Ram Air ???????||||5||
Z||000000||Xtreme Fiero's||01-15-2001||05:10 PM||||<BR>to all who have force fed engines what happens to your Vac. driven acc.'s (Power brakes & Cruise) when there is (+) pressure in the intake? I Know you can run the lines up before the Turbo or S/C to get Vac. but what about real Ram Air? wouldn't any + pressure cause thies systems not to work?||||reg||5
Z||000001||BBBAD GT||01-15-2001||06:22 PM||||I've never had a need for brakes/cruise or anything else when I'm under boost in my 'other two cars', so I guess you can look at it that way.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">     <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||gixxer||01-15-2001||07:20 PM||||On my turbo installation, the PCV and power brakes are pretty much as stock. The power brake cylinder has a one-way check valve already (way up front), the PCV valve will shut under boost also. MY cruise control is electric, 'tho the stock unit will also work under boost also (I presume it has a check valve as well, to keep intake backfires from harming it). Ditto with the carbon canister. <BR>So if you put positive pressure in the intake manifold, all the vacuum systems will see it as a backfire, and protect themselves with check valves.<BR>Did I miss anything?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Xtreme Fiero's||01-15-2001||07:34 PM||||BBBAD GT: Guess I never looked at it like that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Gixxer: does the check engine light come on?||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||01-15-2001||07:59 PM||||On the SC's, the vacuum accessories are supplied from the blower inlet (vacuum), not the outlet (boost).||||reg||1
Z||000005||Xtreme Fiero's||01-15-2001||08:11 PM||||I was thinking moro of True Ram Air. But like BBBad GT said as soon as the Throttle body is colsed wouldn't Vac. return in the manifold, Right?||||reg||1
Z||000006||BBBAD GT||01-15-2001||08:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Xtreme Fiero's:<BR><B>like BBBad GT said as soon as the Throttle body is colsed wouldn't Vac. return in the manifold, Right?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>A better term would be load, as soon as you don't have load on the motor, it goes to vacuum regardless of where the throttle/rpms are.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">     <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||gixxer||01-15-2001||08:55 PM||||As far as I know on my installation, all the vacuum systems use existing ports from the intake manifold. There may be stock vacuum lines going to the air filter can, but I don't think so. <BR>No vacuum sources are used from the intake side of the compressor. This area is busy with the surge/recirculation bypass anyway.<BR>No check engine light has come on so far. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Xtreme Fiero's||01-15-2001||09:18 PM||||I guess i'll find out soon enough. I don't think my Ram Air setup will make enough pressure to affect anything any way. Thanks for the help.||||reg||1
Z||000009||BBBAD GT||01-15-2001||11:23 PM||||I agree, I've never seen a ram air setup pressureize the intake to simulate boost, regardless of the mph traveling (I'm sure there is a point, but I'd guess its over 150 mph).  You won't have any worries.<P>||||reg||1
